  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, Mass of each block A and B, m = 0.1 kg<br /><br />Radius of circle, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Ques_7521_1_1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 199px;\" /><br /><br />The natural length of spring <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">l</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>0.06</mtext> <mi>π</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mi>π</mi> <mtext>R</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;(Half circle) and spring constant,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />In the stretched position elongation in each spring<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>R</mtext> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Let us draw FBD of A<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Ques_7521_1_2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 220px;\" /><br /><br />Spring in lower side is stretched by 2x and on upper side compressed by 2x. Therefore, a force 2kx on each block would be exerted by each spring.<br /><br />Hence, a restoring force, F = 4kx will act on A in the direction shown in figure.<br /><br />Restoring torque of this force about origin<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>τ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>F. R</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>kx</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>R</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>kR</mtext> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>R</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>τ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>kR</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>·</mo> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp; ..... (i)<br /><br />Since, <math> <mrow> <mi>τ</mi> <mo>∝</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math>, each ball executes angular SHM about origin O.<br /><br />Equation. (i) can be written as<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>I</mtext> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>kR</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or &nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>mR</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfenced> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mtext>kR</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or <math> <mrow> <mi>α</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>k</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Frequency of oscillation, <math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> <msqrt> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>acceleration</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>displacement</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </msqrt> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> <msqrt> <mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>α</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </msqrt> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> <msqrt> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>k</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>m</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </msqrt> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Substituting the values, we have<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>f</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> <msqrt> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mtext>0.1</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>0.1</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </msqrt> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>&nbsp;Hz</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
